From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: android-kitkat-tls12 <android-kitkat-tls12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/32] NULL checks in NativeCrypto_SSL_get_ciphers

The port of conscrypt 2d089e18 (libcore/0002) added
NativeCrypto_SSL_get_ciphers as upstream wrote it: neither the
NewLongArray result nor the GetLongArrayElements pointer was checked, so
an allocation failure would write through NULL (a native crash) instead
of leaving the OutOfMemoryError for the caller. Both now return NULL
with the exception pending. No test: the failure needs an exhausted
Java heap.

Android 4.2 port (android-4.2.2_r1) of patch 0029 of the 4.4 series
(renumbered: the 4.4 patch 0025, the ssl.SocketFactory.provider hook of
the TLS 1.3 layer, is not part of this series), made from its Android
4.3 port. 4.2 NativeCrypto_SSL_get_ciphers returns a jintArray (patch
0002): the checks are written for NewIntArray and ScopedIntArrayRW.
---
 ...org_apache_harmony_xnet_provider_jsse_NativeCrypto.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/luni/src/main/native/org_apache_harmony_xnet_provider_jsse_NativeCrypto.cpp b/luni/src/main/native/org_apache_harmony_xnet_provider_jsse_NativeCrypto.cpp
index 06e23f7f65e..e2f62ef0f87 100644
--- a/luni/src/main/native/org_apache_harmony_xnet_provider_jsse_NativeCrypto.cpp
+++ b/luni/src/main/native/org_apache_harmony_xnet_provider_jsse_NativeCrypto.cpp
@@ -3243,7 +3243,15 @@ static jintArray NativeCrypto_SSL_get_ciphers(JNIEnv* env, jclass, jint ssl_addr
     STACK_OF(SSL_CIPHER)* cipherStack = SSL_get_ciphers(ssl);
     int count = (cipherStack != NULL) ? sk_SSL_CIPHER_num(cipherStack) : 0;
     ScopedLocalRef<jintArray> ciphersArray(env, env->NewIntArray(count));
+    if (ciphersArray.get() == NULL) {
+        JNI_TRACE("NativeCrypto_SSL_get_ciphers(%p) => NewIntArray failed", ssl);
+        return NULL;  // OutOfMemoryError pending
+    }
     ScopedIntArrayRW ciphers(env, ciphersArray.get());
+    if (ciphers.get() == NULL) {
+        JNI_TRACE("NativeCrypto_SSL_get_ciphers(%p) => GetIntArrayElements failed", ssl);
+        return NULL;  // OutOfMemoryError pending
+    }
     for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
         ciphers[i] = static_cast<jint>(reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(sk_SSL_CIPHER_value(cipherStack, i)));
     }
